  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tanzania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project includes empowering the TB patient organisation MKUTA and strengthen health systems through Kibongoto Infectious Disease Hospital (KIDH) that specializes in care for people with drug resistant TB, and Temeke Municipality. More than 1 million people are screened annually- specifically targeting key and vulnerable populations based on gender risk analysis such as miners, prisoners and people who use drugs. Other key interventions are treatment support, silicosis screening, lung rehabilitation for people with post TB disability, research and advocacy.</narrative>
  </description>
